1. legitimate DPoP request:
   ACCEPTED 200
2. the same proof replayed:
   REJECTED 401 (DPoP error="invalid_dpop_proof", error_description="The DPoP proof is invalid.")
3. a proof signed with another key (stolen token, wrong key):
   REJECTED 401 (DPoP error="invalid_dpop_proof", error_description="The DPoP proof is invalid.")
4. a proof bound to another HTTP method:
   REJECTED 401 (DPoP error="invalid_dpop_proof", error_description="The DPoP proof is invalid.")
5. the bound token presented as plain Bearer:
   REJECTED: the DPoP-bound token cannot bypass the proof check
6. an unbound legacy token still works over plain Bearer:
   ACCEPTED: unbound legacy token
7. replay storage outage (no Bearer downgrade):
   REJECTED 401 (DPoP error="invalid_dpop_proof", error_description="The DPoP proof is invalid.")
8. a failed request did not consume its jti:
   ACCEPTED 200
